PATCH 0016 -- ath12k: refuse to use the device after a failed resume (no more frozen machine)

On top of 0014 (keep the device across a suspend) and 0015 (re-attach to it).  0015 does not work: the
firmware refuses the QMI firmware start with -22 ("qmi wlan config request failed, result: 1, err: 90"),
ath12k_core_restart() returns before complete(&ab->restart_completed), and ath12k_core_resume() times
out.  What is left behind is worse than a dead radio: ath12k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() has already
deinited the HAL rings and its error path does not rebuild them, while the netdev is still registered.
The next thing to touch it is NetworkManager opening the interface, and the WMI path then walks a
deinited ring:

    Internal error: Oops: 96000007 [#1] SMP
    CPU: 2 PID: 1925 Comm: NetworkManager
    pc : ath12k_hal_srng_access_begin+0x10/0x60 [ath12k]
    lr : ath12k_ce_send+0xcc/0x2c0 [ath12k]
    Call trace: ath12k_htc_send -> ath12k_wmi_cmd_send_nowait -> ath12k_wmi_cmd_send
                -> ath12k_wmi_pdev_set_param -> ath12k_mac_op_start -> drv_start
                -> ieee80211_do_open -> __dev_open -> rtnl_newlink (NetworkManager)
    (measured 2026-09-22 10:13, kernel-tail.log)

followed by "watchdog: BUG: soft lockup - CPU#1 stuck for 23s", which is what the operator sees as a
machine frozen with no keyboard and no touchpad.

Fix: set ATH12K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH when the resume times out.  That is the driver's own "the firmware is
gone, do not touch the hardware" state -- ath12k_ce_send() checks it before it touches the ring and
returns -ESHUTDOWN, wmi maps it to -ESHUTDOWN, the data path, peer, thermal and mac80211 paths all
check it too.  A failed resume now degrades to "no WiFi until a reboot" instead of taking the machine
down with it, which is also what makes 'sudo ~/a16.sh radiofix revive' (re-probe the PCI function
without rebooting) usable as a recovery.

Also corrects the MHI state text in the 0014 log line: 0x1 is M0 and 0x2 is M1 (both are mission mode),
the earlier "0x2 = M0" label was wrong.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
